<title>JAPAN: Moody's sees growing ratings gap among Japan banks.</title>
<headline>Moody's sees growing ratings gap among Japan banks.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-03-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Moody's Investors Service said on Tuesday it expects the gap between the credit ratings of weaker and stronger Japanese banks to widen as Japan's financial markets continue their rapid shift to a more liberalised and competitive environment.</p>
<p>Over the next three to five years, Moody's expects the Japanese banking system's overall ratings to remain near current levels but the rating differential between individual banks is likely to expand, it said in a statement.</p>
</text>
